 ## Background
-The field of NeRF editing emerged as NeRFs gained popularity for novel view synthesis, with early works focusing on simple object removal or colorization. The integration of 2D diffusion models (e.g., Stable Diffusion) as priors for 3D editing became prominent around 2023, leading to methods like Instruct-NeRF2NeRF and RePaint-NeRF. Recent developments include semantic-guided editing, sparse-view inpainting, and hybrid approaches combining 3D Gaussian Splatting with diffusion priors. These methods are widely used in virtual production, augmented reality, and 3D content creation.
+The field of NeRF editing emerged as NeRFs gained popularity for novel view synthesis, with early works focusing on object removal and scene manipulation. Key developments include the introduction of diffusion-guided editing (e.g., RePaint-NeRF, Instruct-NeRF2NeRF) which leveraged 2D generative models to guide 3D optimization [14365-repaint-nerf.md, 15089-instruct-nerf2nerf-optimization.md]. Subsequent methods like Blended-NeRF and NeRF-Art introduced techniques for localized editing and stylization using text prompts and volumetric blending [12273-blended-nerf.md, 13438-nerf-art.md]. Recent advancements focus on improving multi-view consistency through semantic priors and progressive inpainting strategies [8658-progressive-inpainting-and-erasing.md, 14393-semantic-and-language-guided-editing.md].
 
